			"text": "From and To are automatically detected based on the following rules. Sort all active releases newest-first: [15, 14, 13, 10] Resolve To - scan from index 0 for the first release where every PROD environment succeeded If To resolved at index > 0, From is index - 1 (the next newer release) If To resolved at index = 0 (the newest release is itself already PROD-complete), there's nothing newer to be From. Slide-back check is applied: - From is index 0 - To is ProdIndexFrom(1) - scan from index 1 for the next PROD-complete release (note that any releases that are not complete - failed, cancelled, etc. - are skipped until next PROD is found) Given above sample, Release 10 is the last, most recent release that every environment is complete. Release 13 would be the first available release after even though it has a canceled PROD environment it is still eligible to redeploy. Choose explicit release numbers with the From and To pickers in the Release Pipeline or Release Differences section head when you need a specific comparison. The pickers are filled with active releases, mark the auto-resolved release with (auto), and commit a selection immediately. Alt+F and Alt+T open the page and focus those controls. If a saved or restored choice cannot be resolved, the Release Pipeline and Release Differences sections render an amber Unavailable state with the range pickers still available so you can choose an active release. Comparison UnavailableThe following cases can result in a grey Nothing to compare or amber Unavailable state: no PROD-complete release yet (brand new pipeline) or only a single PROD-complete release with nothing to compare against."
