			"text": "The default cap is 10,000 result rows (Settings allows 1 to 100,000). If it is reached, Grazer stops and marks the results incomplete. The default size cap is 50 MB (1 to 256 MB): ordinary files and ZIP containers are bounded by on-disk size; ZIP entries are bounded by uncompressed size. Oversized, binary or unreadable content is skipped with a visible reason. Text is read as UTF-8 first; a file with no byte-order mark that is not valid UTF-8 is searched again as Windows-1252, so older ANSI sources still match. Only files whose encoding cannot be read either way count as unsupported or malformed. Shared repositories are often cloned under several sites. With Search each Shared repository once on in Settings (the default), the first copy of each Shared* repository found is searched and later copies are skipped and counted as duplicate Shared repositories. Turn it off to search every copy. ZIP searching is off by default and can only be enabled in Settings. When enabled, matching text entries are read without extracting them; archives and their entries are never modified. Searching .git metadata is a separate Settings option and is off by default. Directory-name, literal excluded-folder and path-fragment lists are editable there, so exclusions are visible rather than hidden filters. Results stay hidden until a search returns, and appear in the page itself rather than in a scrolling box. They form a tree of repository folder, file and matching line (in file or folder modes, folder and file or folder leaf), with a badge of matching lines on each row and a summary line under the header. Hover a row to dismiss it; dismissing a line, file or folder removes it from the current result set and from replacement, and a folder disappears once its last child is dismissed. A new search, including F5, restores dismissed matches."
