			"text": "The refreshes you reach for most often have keys. F5 Refreshes the whole site: every section, and the rail's badges with them. On Tools > Grazer, re-runs the last submitted search; before the first accepted search, it does nothing. On Tools > Repository Status, rescans the roots and checks every repository's local status, without fetching; use Ctrl+F5, or Ctrl+Click, there for a manual fetch. See Refreshing. Ctrl+Shift+W Re-runs every saved Work Items query, the same as the ↻ in the Work Items header: the rail's query counts and the results of the query that is open. Ctrl+Shift+Q Re-runs just the open query. With no query open, it does nothing. Ctrl+Shift+R Refreshes the Release Pipeline, the Release Pipeline KPI tile, and Release Differences together, because all three come from one fetch. Ctrl+Shift+C Refreshes the CalcEngine Pipeline. On a site with no CalcEngine patterns there is no section to refresh, so the key does nothing."
