			"title": "Keyboard Shortcuts",
			"heading": "Access keys",
			"text": "The site picker in the app bar, and the From/To pickers and CalcEngine Patterns box in the section headers, have access keys. Press and release Alt on its own to underline their letters; press it again, or click anywhere, to hide them. Like the refresh shortcuts, they are ignored while a dialog is open - a dialog uses Alt for its own fields. Alt+S Opens the site picker with its search box focused. Type to narrow the list, ↑/↓ (or Page Up/Page Down) to move, Enter to load the highlighted site and Esc to close it without changing anything. With the closed picker focused, typing a letter opens it with that letter already searched. Alt+F / Alt+T Focus the From or To release picker, switching to the Release Pipeline page first. Picking a release refreshes the Release Pipeline straight away; there is nothing further to press. Alt+C Focus CalcEngine Patterns, switching to the CalcEngine Pipeline page first. Press Enter in the box to refresh the CalcEngine Pipeline with the new patterns. Nothing else is re-fetched."
