			"title": "Keyboard Shortcuts",
			"heading": "Work Items grid",
			"text": "With a query open, the grid can be driven from the keyboard without reaching for the mouse. The keys match GitHub's, so they should already be in your fingers. They also work when focus is on a button - after clicking a rail entry or a header button, for instance - so you do not have to click back into the grid first. The exception is when you are typing in a box, such as the site search or a filter box, where a letter means what it always means. Navigation j Move down one row, wrapping from the last row back to the first. With nothing selected yet, selects the first row. k Move up one row, wrapping from the first row round to the last. With nothing selected yet, selects the last row. o / Enter Open the selected row's work item detail - the same thing clicking its title does. Does nothing when no row is selected. Esc Leaves Return Triage Tasks select mode if it is active; otherwise unselects the currently selected row. With both, the first press leaves select mode and the second unselects the row. Actions - Grid focused All actions open 'edit' dialog for a task's Assigned To, Comment, State and Triage. These same actions are also available on each row's Context Menu. c Add Comment to the selected row. Defaults: Comment = Default Comment Text. r Return Task to previous owner. Defaults: Triage = Pending, Reassign To = previous owner, Comment = Default Return Task Comment. t Triage Task. Defaults: Triage = Triaged, Comment = Default Triage Comment. x Close Task. Defaults: State = Closed, Comment = Default Close Task Comment. Return Triaged Tasks Space Tick or untick the selected row's checkbox while a batch workflow is active."
