			"text": "Besides F5 (see above), the Tools > Repository Status table, its menus and its dialogs work from the keyboard. Each row's … actions button is always there, so Tab reaches it. Enter / Space / → / ← On a focused repository row, Enter or Space expands or collapses it to show its branches and worktrees; → expands and ← collapses. Expansion and focus survive background checks. ↓ / Enter on … or ▾ Opens a row's actions menu, or the Batch Action menu, with its first available item focused. ↑/↓ and Home/End move, → opens a remote's Fetch / Push / Force Push entries and ← closes them, Enter chooses, and Esc closes the menu and returns focus to its button. Pressing the button again also closes it. Space on a row checkbox In batch mode, ticks or clears that row; All in the header does every applicable row on screen. Continue runs the batch action, Cancel leaves batch mode, and so does Esc while you are still choosing rows; once the action is running, Cancel stops it instead. Esc in a dialog Cancels the Pull preview, the Commit / Push review, the worktree cleanup review or a confirmation, changes nothing (a \"Don't ask me\" switch is saved only when you confirm), and returns focus to the control that opened it. Ctrl+Enter in the commit message Confirms the Commit / Push review, like its button. Enter alone starts a new line."
