			"title": "Version 2.1",
			"heading": "Search local folders with Grazer",
			"text": "Find the same setting, phrase or old name across your local folders without opening each project. Grazer, under Tools, searches multiple literal terms together, with a case / whole word setting for each. Review matching lines grouped by folder and file, or switch to file or folder names for a broader view. Searches run only when you ask, never while you type or on a timer. For replacements, each changed line shows its Old and New text before you write. Apply changes to a line, file or folder, or use Replace All; dismiss matches you want to leave alone. Grazer re-reads files before writing and refuses files changed since the search, preserving their encoding and line endings. ZIP entries, when ZIP searching is enabled, remain read-only. No backup files are created, so keep changes under source control. See Grazer in Help. Preview every replacement before writing, from a single line to Replace All."
