			"title": "Version 2.1",
			"heading": "KCC Improvements",
			"text": "In the Work Items grid, press Enter to open the selected work item, just like o. See Keyboard Shortcuts. Work Item updates now protect against stale saves. If an item changed after its dialog opened, nothing is overwritten: the current item is refreshed, the dialog preserves anything you typed for copying, and unaffected items in a batch can still be saved. See Work Items. Return Triaged now shows the selected count and progress in a batch action strip. Failed items are listed above the grid, with Retry reopening only those items and preserving the values you submitted. Return Task requires an assignee, and Move to Triaged requires a Triage value. See Return Triage Tasks. Work Item query badges now explain their count as the number of distinct items flagged by your thresholds, rather than a breakdown that could count an item more than once. See Rail badges. Authentication is more resilient for DataLocker, CalcEngine, and Site Scope. Saved credentials are retained through expired tokens and temporary service or network failures so a later refresh can sign in again automatically; credentials are cleared only when the service actually rejects them, and unexpected failures now report their real error instead of looking like a bad password. See CalcEngine and Site Scope."
